

<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
A man takes <m>3</m> seconds to breathe in and out once. The volume of air in his lungs, <m>V(t)</m>, varies between a minimum of <m>0.5</m> liters and a maximum of <m>4.5</m> liters. Assume that at time <m>t=0</m> the volume is at a minimum; that is, time <m>t=0</m> is when the man begins to breathe in.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
What are the period, amplitude, and midline of <m>V(t)</m>?
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The period is <m>3</m> seconds. The amplitude is
<md>
\text{Amp. } \quad=\quad \frac{y_\text{max} -y_\text{min} }{2} \quad = \quad  \frac{4.5-0.5}{2}  \quad = \quad 2 \text{ liters}.
</md> The midline equation is
<md>
y \quad = \quad \frac{y_\text{max}  + y_\text{min} }{2}  \quad = \quad \frac{4.5+0.5}{2}  \quad = \quad 2.5.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
Sketch a possible graph of <m>V(t)</m> which shows two periods of <m>V(t)</m>.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The graph is given below.
</p>

\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.7]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style = very thick,
xmin=0,xmax=6,
ymin=0,ymax=5,
xtick={3,6},
ytick={0.5,2.5,4.5},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(t\), ylabel=\(V(t)\),
trig format plots = rad,
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=0:6 ,thick] {-2*cos(2*3.14159*x/3)+2.5};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

</solution>
</task>



</exercise>


<exercise workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
Estimate the period of the following periodic function <m>f(t)</m>:
</p>


\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|} \hline
$t$ & $0$ & $1$ & $2$ & $3$ & $4$ & $5$ & $6$ \\\hline
$f(t)$ & $12$ & $13$ & $14$ & $12$ & $13$ & $14$ & $12$ \\\hline
\end{tabular}


</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The outputs <m>12</m>, <m>13</m>, <m>14</m> are repeating in this pattern. And, it takes <m>3</m> units of <m>x</m> to do so, therefore the period of this function is <m>3</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>



<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
Estimate the period of the following periodic function <m>g(x)</m>:
</p>


\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|} \hline
$x$ & $1$ & $11$ & $21$ & $31$ & $41$ & $51$ & $61$ & $71$ & $81$ \\\hline
$g(x)$ & $5$ & $3$ & $2$ & $3$ & $5$ & $3$ & $2$ & $3$ & $5$ \\\hline
\end{tabular}


</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The outputs <m>5</m>, <m>3</m>, <m>2</m>, <m>3</m> are repeating in this pattern. And, it takes <m>40</m> units of <m>x</m> to do so, therefore the period is <m>40</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>




<exercise workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
For the graphs (A) -- (D) below, identify which could be periodic functions.
</p>


\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{CC}
(A) & (B) \\[1em]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style = very thick,
xmin=-10,xmax=11,
ymin=-5, ymax=5,
xtick={-6.28,-3.14,3.14,6.28,9.425},
xticklabels = {-2,-1,1,2,3},
xticklabel style = {xshift=0.2cm},
ytick={-3.751,3.751},
yticklabels = {-3,3},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(f(x)\),
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=-8.64:10 ,thick] {1.3*(2*sin(deg(x)) - sin(deg(2*x)) + 0.6666*sin(deg(3*x)))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
&
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
xmin=0,xmax=5,
axis line style = very thick,
ymin=-5,ymax=5,
xtick={1,2,3,4},
xticklabel style = {xshift=0.2cm},
ytick={-4,-2,2,4},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(f(x)\),
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=0:5 ,thick] {4*sin(deg(3.14159*x))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\\[2em]
(C) & (D) \\[2em]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style = very thick,
xmin=-3,xmax=4,
ymin=-2,ymax=2,
xtick=\empty,
ytick=\empty,
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(f(x)\),
samples=300]
\addplot[domain=-3:3.7 ,thick] {sin(deg(e^(1.1*x)))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
&
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style = very thick,
xmin=-1,xmax=16,
ymin=-5,ymax=5,
xtick=\empty,
ytick=\empty,
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(f(x)\),
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=0:15 ,thick] {e^(0.1*\x) * sin(deg(3*\x))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{tabularx}


</statement>

<solution>
<p>
Graphs (A) and (B) are periodic meanwhile (C) and (D) are not.
</p>

<p>
In graph (C), the outputs are oscillating between the same numbers but the length of a cycle is constantly changing (always getting smaller). 
</p>

<p>
In graph (D), the outputs are not oscillating between the same values. That is, the amplitude is appearing to grow as <m>x</m> increases.
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>




<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
Estimate the period of each of the functions depicted below.
</p>

\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style = very thick,
xmin=-5,xmax=5,
ymin=-2.5,ymax=2.5,
xtick={-4,-2,2,4},
ytick={-2,2},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(f(x)\),
trig format plots = rad,
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=-5:5 ,thick] {2*cos(2*3.14159*x/4)};

\ifprintanswers
\addplot[domain=0:4 ,very thick,red] {2*cos(2*3.14159*x/4)};
\else \fi
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}


\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style = very thick,
xmin=-5,xmax=5,
ymin=-1.5,ymax=1.5,
xtick={-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4},
xticklabel style = {xshift=0.2cm},
ytick={-1,1},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(f(x)\),
trig format plots = rad,
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=-5:5 ,thick] {sin(2*3.14159*x/2)};

\ifprintanswers
\addplot[domain=0:2 ,very thick,red] {sin(2*3.14159*x/2)};
\else \fi
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The first graph has a period of <m>4</m> and the second graph has a period of <m>2</m>. An <em>example</em> of one cycle is shown on the graphs to illustrate this.
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>

